Yet Another Great Save...

(There is no god but the RNG and Izchak is the prophet of the RNG.  Knock on
simulated woodgrain just for good measure.)

My game in progress on NAO is an archaeologist.  I fought my way down to
level 5 and stepped on a level teleporter.  I wound up on level 6...in a
room with 3 wolves, and me at experience level 7, 46 HP and AC 4.  Time to
back up into a hallway.

I whack the first wolf.  It dies...and I'm down to 3 HP.  Time to pray.

I whack the second wolf.  It dies.  I have maybe 12 HP this time, and
praying is out of the question.  Time to retreat into unknown parts of the
dungeon.

Alas, the corridor leads to a room with no other exit.  No door in the
doorway.  And that third wolf is still after my hide.

I reach into my sack.  There are two black potions, unidentified and
unaltarized.  Nothing else looks like it could help.

Well, sometimes you just have to roll the dice....

"You feel better."

I manage to take care of the third wolf.  Looking for the up-stairs, I step
on a trap door.  I wind up on level 9...in a room with up-stairs.

Up-stairs, that is, to Sokoban.

All praise to the RNG.

